Z||000001||Uaana||12-14-2001||03:00 PM||||I'm running their Sixron 4's <BR>Great deal for the price. Not the stickiest but great in rain. <BR>Only real problem I've had is they are designed to run at 50-55psi and if one tire goes down a little you really feel it. (car kinda wander's / floats)||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroKyle||12-14-2001||08:10 PM||||I'll just stick to my Goodyears.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierochild||12-14-2001||08:31 PM||||I've had a set of their 17" HTR Z II on my car since Feb.  215/40 in back and 205 40s up front.  These are my street tires.  I usually run Hoosiers for autocross.  On a couple of occasions I had to run with my street tires.  No comparison to the Hoosiers, but a whole lot better than the Kellys that came with the car.  I've got about 3000 miles on them and they show very little wear.  Ride is firm and for the price they handle good.  I bought mine through the tire rack.  My wheels are Team Loco 17X7s.  Look pretty decent for less than $600.  As for the tires, I will probably buy another set when these wear out.<P>Chuck<BR>Lambo green 86GT <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierochildsig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierochild (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
